From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:15:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [ofono] Fix call state, direction, duration and start time
 reporting.

- A call let through by the call filter reported STATUS_INCOMING again
  once it ended, as "disconnected" fell into the filter mapping. Every
  incoming call goes through it when no filter plugin is loaded, so MCE
  went back to "ringing" and commhistory never saw the call end. Only
  map "disconnected" to the filter's verdict for ignored and rejected
  calls.
- Calls waiting behind another call were reported as outgoing, so they
  were logged as dialled. ofono's "waiting" is mobile terminated as
  well. Decide the direction once: ofono coming back mid-call made the
  handler valid again in state "active".
- durationChanged() carried the duration in milliseconds, truncated to
  int, while duration() is in seconds. The QML duration jumped to a
  thousand times the right value on the first tick.
- startedAt() parsed ofono's StartTime with an empty format and was
  never valid, and startedAtChanged() was never emitted. Parse the ISO
  8601 time with its +HHMM offset and emit on changes.
- Asynchronous dial failures were dropped: dialComplete() wasn't
  connected and the provider's error() was never emitted.
- When the modem lost its VoiceCallManager interface, calls still
  waiting for their properties were kept with a pointer to the deleted
  manager, used later by answer(), hold() and sendDtmf(). Delete them
  with it, and hold the manager in a QPointer. A repeated callAdded for
  such a call created a second handler.
- A call whose properties were known when its handler was created was
  never announced: the handler signalled validity from its constructor,
  before the provider connected to it.

Add a unit test of the provider and handler against stand-ins for the
libqofono classes.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
